Step 1: Set Up the Next.js Project
Install Next.js: Start by creating a new Next.js project. Open your terminal and run the following command:

bash
Copy code
npx create-next-app pub-comparison
cd pub-comparison
Install Dependencies: Depending on your requirements, you might need additional libraries. For example, if you need to fetch data from an API, you might use Axios or similar libraries. For styling, you might use Tailwind CSS or styled-components.

bash
Copy code
npm install axios
npm install tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p
Configure Tailwind CSS: If you’re using Tailwind CSS, add the following to your tailwind.config.js:

javascript
Copy code
/** @type {import('tailwindcss').Config} */
module.exports = {
  content: [
    './pages/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}',
    './components/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}',
  ],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  plugins: [],
};
And add the Tailwind directives to your styles/globals.css:

css
Copy code
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;
